# Repo overview

## Layout
- `backend/` — Express + TypeScript + Prisma (primary API/worker); deploy on **VPS** via `scripts/deploy.sh`
- `frontend/` — Next.js 15 App Router dashboard (port **3001**); deploy on **Vercel** (git push only)
- `docs/` — `docs/deployment.md`, `docs/v3-operations.md`, `docs/api-spec.md`, `docs/architecture.md`
- `scripts/deploy.sh` — VPS backend rollout (PM2 reload + health check)
- `backend-go/` — separate Go service; do not assume it when editing Node backend unless the task says so
- `frontend-old/` — legacy Vite app; avoid unless migrating

## Stack (verified)
- DB: **PostgreSQL** via Prisma (`backend/prisma/schema.prisma`, `DATABASE_URL`)
- API: Express 4, entry `backend/src/server.ts` (HTTP) and `backend/src/worker.ts` (cron/schedulers)
- Process split: `API_ONLY` / `WORKER_ONLY` — never run conflicting roles in one production process
- Frontend: React 19, Tailwind, path aliases `@/*`, `@/lib/*`, `@/app/*`

## Global coding rules
- Match `strict: true` in both `tsconfig.json` files; avoid `any` on public APIs, DTOs, and props
- Smallest safe change; reuse existing modules before new abstractions
- No new dependencies unless required
- Do not invent env vars, endpoints, or models — read `backend/.env.example`, routes, and Prisma schema first
- Trading domain: preserve `method_id` (`ict` preserved/disabled, `kim_nghia` active); keep `bias` / `action` / `side` consistent
- Long: `stop_loss < entry < take_profit`; short: `take_profit < entry < stop_loss`
- Docs may lag code; prefer `backend/src/config`, live routes, and Prisma over stale README claims (e.g. SQLite-only)

## Commands
- Backend dev: `cd backend && npm run dev` (API), `npm run dev:worker` (worker)
- Backend build/test: `npm run build`, `npm test` / `npm run test:run`
- VPS deploy: `~/deploy.sh` or `./scripts/deploy.sh` (backend only; see `docs/deployment.md`)
- Frontend dev: `cd frontend && npm run dev` (production: Vercel auto-build on push)
